---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: Features
eyebrow: Product
subtitle: Every capability Project Broadsheet ships with, organized the way you'd evaluate one.
permalink: /features/
---
<div class="features-intro lead">
  Project Broadsheet isn't a theme or a minimal starter. It's a full publication framework with everything an indie newsroom, newsletter, or small magazine needs, and nothing bolted on just to check a marketing box.
</div>

<section class="section-sm" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);">
  <h2 class="h3" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);">Who uses it</h2>
  <div class="grid grid-2" style="max-width: 52rem;">
    <div>
      <strong>Independent journalists</strong>
      <p style="color: var(--text-soft); margin-top: 0.25rem;">A full newsroom platform for a publication of one. Sections, corrections, source documents, RSS, and reader tools without a platform subscription.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <strong>Student newspapers</strong>
      <p style="color: var(--text-soft); margin-top: 0.25rem;">Campus and classroom publications that teach real editorial workflows — version control, corrections, structured content — at no recurring cost to the institution.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <strong>Academic researchers</strong>
      <p style="color: var(--text-soft); margin-top: 0.25rem;">Citation formatters (APA, MLA, Chicago), primary source documents, argument maps, and a public-domain library built for scholarly publishing.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <strong>Nonprofit newsrooms</strong>
      <p style="color: var(--text-soft); margin-top: 0.25rem;">Community news outlets and public-interest publishers. MIT-licensed, no platform revenue share, full ownership of content and code.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% for f in features.highlights %}
<section class="feature-block" id="{{ f.title | slugify }}">
  <div class="feature-block__grid">
    <header class="feature-block__header">
      <span class="eyebrow">{{ loop.index | string | replace('0','0') }} · {{ f.title }}</span>
      <h2>{{ f.title }}</h2>
      <p class="feature-block__summary">{{ f.summary }}</p>
    </header>
    <ul class="feature-block__list">
      {% for point in f.points %}<li>{{ point }}</li>{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
{% endfor %}

<section class="section">
  <div class="grid grid-4">
    {% for s in features.stats %}
    <div class="stat-card">
      <div class="stat-card__value">{{ s.value }}</div>
      <div class="stat-card__label">{{ s.label }}</div>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>
